            <ArticleTitle>[Acute coronary artery dissection after aortic valve replacement].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e23-5, e82-5, e31-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0066-782X2010000200026</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Late aortic dissection can occur after aortic valve replacement surgery, but rarely in the first postoperative month. Coronary artery dissection is rare and usually occurs after coronary angiography. We report a rare case of coronary artery dissection followed by myocardial infarction in the immediate postoperative period of a successful aortic valve replacement with a good postoperative evolution.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
